Introduction of UNGA 80 Third Committee Amendment to Resolution: “Strengthening the United Nations crime prevention and criminal justice program, in particular its technical cooperation capacity”
Kali Gasteiger
U.S. Adviser to the Third Committee
New York, New York
AS DELIVERED
Thank you, Mr. Chair, The United States supports strong enforcement of criminal law against all forms of “child sexual abuse material” or “child pornography,” and supports this amendment, including to clarify that the parameters for UNODC’s cooperation with States are to be in line with the Optional Protocol to the Convention on the Rights of the Child on the Sale of Children, Child Prostitution, and Child Pornography. We therefore strongly urge all Member States to join in adopting this important amendment. Thank you.
