Ambassador Mike Waltz
U.S. Representative to the United Nations
New York, New York
AS DELIVERED
Thank you, Mr. President. Thank you, Director Gotoh, Director Wosornu, for your briefings today.
Colleagues, we have yet another winter approaching – Ukraine’s fourth since Russia launched its invasion – and it is imperative to end this war and begin the process of rebuilding. Colleagues, diplomacy is the only, it is the only path to a durable and just peace.
The United States has invested at the highest levels, the President of the United States personally, to end this war. We have proposed generous terms for Russia, including sanctions relief. We have asked Russia to halt its attacks and meet directly with Ukraine to negotiate a peaceful settlement.
Unfortunately, the fighting continues. Tragically, causing more civilian casualties, and we’ve also seen incursions now into the airspace of third countries, including of our NATO Allies – actions that risk widening this conflict even further.
Ukraine’s counterattacks in turn have hit Russia’s energy sector and other critical infrastructure, further constraining Russia’s ability to fuel its war economy. And Russia has now suffered more than a million casualties. It has endured severe international sanctions.
Colleagues, the bottom line is the cost to all sides have been devastating. And it is beyond time for this war to end. And I would hope that we would all agree that this war will not end militarily. Russia’s and Ukraine’s leaders must negotiate. Both Russia and Ukraine must accept a ceasefire.
Further, the U.S. – from the international community standpoint – the U.S. has called on all countries, particularly those in Europe, to stop buying energy resources from Russia. And we have imposed additional sanctions on Russia’s two largest oil companies, Rosneft and Lukoil. We did so on October 22. We can impose further economic costs if Russia continues to ignore calls for a ceasefire.
We will also continue to make weapons available for Ukraine’s defense.
Colleagues, finally, we cannot let this meeting pass without calling for the return of the kidnapped and missing children from Ukraine, for the resolution of that issue.
And colleagues, under President Trump’s leadership, the United States will continue to pursue a path to peace in Ukraine. We ask all UN member states to join us in supporting these efforts, calling for a ceasefire, and ending this war.
I thank you.
