New York, New York
AS DELIVERED
Thank you, Mr. Chair,
The United States is proud to bring this resolution before the committee for consideration. This resolution is proof that the cause of protecting and promoting human rights around the world is not only a noble endeavor, but one that is practically attainable even in parts of the world that many consider their advancement currently impossible.
For a decade, this resolution served to ensure that the human rights abuses perpetrated by the Assad regime would not go unchallenged – that the purposes and principles of the Charter of the United Nations and other relevant international instruments safeguarding human rights were not diminished as a consequence of the Assad regime’s abuses against its own citizens.
Now, however, this body has the privileged opportunity to turn a new page and instead use this resolution to welcome the Syrian Government’s repeated statements and commitments since December of last year to not only bring perpetrators to justice, but ensure that the rights guaranteed under international law to all in Syria are enshrined and upheld by the new Syrian Government.
The United States stands ready to support Syria in this new chapter of its history. We will continue to work with our counterparts in government to help the Syrian people forge a free and open civil society for all Syrians.
Mr. Chair, we are hopeful that this resolution, for the first time since its introduction more than a decade ago, will be adopted by consensus – a powerful message of this body’s solidarity with the Syrian people.
