Ambassador Jeff Bartos
U.S. Representative for U.N. Management and Reform
New York, New York
AS DELIVERED
The United States wishes to deliver an explanation of vote on the six resolutions put forward today.
The United States remains unwavering in its commitment to Israel’s security, the demilitarization of Gaza, and President Trump’s vision of peace and prosperity for the whole region – a vision backed by our partners in the region.
Colleagues, year after year, this package of one-sided, anti-Israel resolutions is put before the committee.
Today, just two days after the historic passing of Resolution 2803 – wherein the UN Security Council overwhelmingly endorsed the President’s Comprehensive Plan – today’s exercise is more absurd than ever.
These resolutions are a sideshow that, now more than ever, serve only to distract from serious diplomatic efforts with the parties on the ground towards peace in the region. To support the latter, we should end business as usual in this chamber and embrace the fresh thinking and bold action through which President Trump ended the war in Gaza and achieved the historic Abraham Accords.
President Trump, through his Plan for Peace, has presented us with a historic opportunity that offers real hope for the people of Gaza. It offers hope for the wider Middle East to turn the page and usher in a new age of peace and prosperity.
This also means turning a page in the region’s history and doing things in a different way. In this respect, the United States opposes the renewal of the UNRWA mandate. As Secretary Rubio said, UNRWA became a subsidiary of Hamas.
All Member States should be joining together in support of the Plan for Peace rather than wasting UN resources through days of considering these resolutions. Let us look to the future. The Security Council resolution adopted on Monday provides the path forward for concrete action by the international community and demonstrates its commitment to the project of peace.
Thank you.
