Thank you, Mr. Chair,
The United States is pleased to co-sponsor and vote in support of this important resolution. The resolution expresses the very serious concern that the DPRK regime continues to restrict the exercise of human rights in the DPRK, in direct opposition to the purposes and principles of the Charter of the United Nations, and other relevant international instruments.
The resolution also expresses grave concern about the exacerbation of the humanitarian situation in the DPRK due to the policies and practices of the regime that cause its people to endure avoidable hardship and suffering, including malnutrition. The regime’s repression serves to advance its unlawful weapons of mass destruction and ballistic missile programs including through the use of forced labor facilities.
The regime diverts a disproportionate amount of its resources into these weapons programs, prioritizing them over the welfare of its people. The actions of the DPRK regime show that human rights violations and abuses are linked to international peace and security. The United States remains committed to diplomacy and dialogue with the DPRK to address these and other concerns.
