Stefanie Williams
Deputy Assistant Secretary for Professional and Cultural Exchanges Bureau of Educational and Cultural Affairs
New York, New York
AS DELIVERED
Good morning. Thank you, Madam President.
I’m honored to represent the United States in the General Assembly today. It’s wonderful to join colleagues from the U.S. Olympic and Paralympic Committee, including Board Chair Gene Sykes.
I’d like to acknowledge and thank our Italian colleagues, including Milano Cortina 2026 President Giovanni Malagò and his team’s tremendous work preparing for the upcoming Winter Games.
It’s also a pleasure to be joined here today by International Olympic Committee President, Kirsty Coventry. The United States appreciates her leadership and the IOC’s efforts to advance peace and fair competition through sport.
As the host country of the 2028 Summer Olympic and Paralympic Games, the United States is excited to welcome the Olympic flame back to U.S. soil and committed to promoting peace and global stability through sport in Los Angeles and again in 2034 when we host the Winter Games in Salt Lake City, Utah.
We believe sports have an unrivaled power to build bridges, foster dialogue, and establish lasting ties among people, among communities, and among nations.
The three core values of the Olympics: Excellence, friendship, and respect, are not only important tenants for the Olympic Games, but also for the United Nations and all member states.
We applaud the Italian government and the Milano Cortina 2026 Organizing Committee for their dedication to an event that catalyzes innovation and provides a platform for safe and fair competition among nations.
We look forward to close collaboration with our Italian counterparts as we work toward hosting the world for the 2028 Summer Games, and later the 2034 Winter Games. Like our Italian colleagues, we are dedicated to ensuring the best Olympic and Paralympic Games possible.
Hosting such a massive event is no small feat, and we are tremendously fortunate to have the opportunity to learn from our Italian partners.
We are excited to celebrate their success and look forward to continued close collaboration as we prepare to host the 2028 Games.
Thank you, Madam President.
