Maria Apud
U.S. Adviser to the Third Committee
New York, New York
AS DELIVERED
Thank you, Mr. Chair,
The United States has made clear its objection to resolutions, such as this one, that are effectively performative and wasteful of UN resources.
Third Committee resolutions should be short, actionable, and forward-looking. Instead, this resolution continues to include problematic language that does nothing to advance the United Nations’ core mandate of maintaining international peace and security.
President Trump has delivered a very clear message: that the United Nations and so many nations of the world have gotten wildly off track, exaggerating climate change into the world’s greatest threat. This practice will no longer be tolerated.
The UN can no longer afford to waste its resources where there is little or no impact. The number of reports, conferences, and negotiations has grown beyond the point of ineffectiveness and waste, to a level of dysfunction that makes it impossible to carry out vital work.
Accordingly, the United States will vote “no” on this resolution.
Mr. Chair, colleagues, we hope to work together in advance of next year’s session of the Third Committee to make it more efficient, relevant, and effective. We refer you to the long form Explanation of Position that will be posted on our Mission’s website for more information. Thank you.
