AS DELIVERED
Thank you, Mr. Chair,
The United States is pleased to vote yes on this resolution. We thank the Denmark delegation for their work in shepherding this. While the United States is voting yes on this resolution, there are some inclusions in the text we wish to disassociate ourselves from.
We disassociate ourselves from preamble paragraph four, “Recognizing the important work carried out by the Human Rights Committee in providing guidance with respect to the scope of freedom of religion or belief,” as the United States does not support the work of the UN Human Rights Committee.
We also disassociate ourselves from the inclusion of the term “Islamophobia” as used in Operative Paragraph four and the inclusion of the term “cultural diversity” in Operative Paragraph 15.
Finally, the United States finds the reference to the United Nations Alliance of Civilizations initiative in Operative Paragraph 16 problematic. We therefore disassociate ourselves from its inclusion.
Mr. Chair, colleagues, we hope to work together in advance of next year’s session of the Third Committee to make it more efficient, relevant, and effective. Thank you.
